-- src:785 | (nếu có).
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`13.2 does not say what follows when the earlier payments for the same illness exceed the middle-stage benefit` MEANS
    REFUSE "13.2 does not say what follows when the earlier payments for the same illness exceed the middle-stage benefit"

GIVEN sa    IS A NUMBER
      other IS A NUMBER
      same  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`13.2(a) — the middle-stage benefit on a sum insured of` sa `, with` other `paid under other contracts and` same `paid for the same illness` MEANS
    IF   `before the deduction` AT LEAST same
    THEN `before the deduction` MINUS same
    ELSE `13.2 does not say what follows when the earlier payments for the same illness exceed the middle-stage benefit`
    WHERE
        `before the deduction` MEANS max 0 (min (50% TIMES sa) (`13.2 — the middle-stage cap` MINUS other))

-- 13.3(a): 100% of the sum insured at the diagnosis, less every early- and middle-stage
-- benefit paid before for the same critical illness. No cap.
