§§ `Article 16 — How the comfort cash coupon and dividends are paid`
-- src:963 | ĐIỀU 16  PHƯƠNG THỨC CHI TRẢ QUYỀN LỢI
-- src:964 | PHIẾU TIỀN MẶT AN NHÀN VÀ BẢO TỨC

DECLARE `A method of payment` IS ONE OF
    `left with the Company at interest`
    `paid in cash at once`
    `applied to premiums as they fall due`

-- 16.1: the coupon first pays off any Debt; the rest, if any, as the policyholder chooses:
-- (i) left with the Company at the published interest rate, withdrawable at any time, or
-- (ii) in cash; (i) if no choice is made. 16.2: a dividend may also be left to pay premiums.
-- 16.3: (i) by default; a choice for one dividend holds for the later ones until changed.
